WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.300
-Today is Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.667
when I catch up
with some personal stuff.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:05.868
You know, I check my inbox,
return some e-mails,

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:08.033
and, of course, send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:09.667
And I was just --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:11.767
I was running a bit behind
today, so I thought,

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:12.968
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:00:12.968 --> 00:00:14.601
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:17.033
Is that cool with you guys?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:20.033
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:26.567
♪♪

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:29.234
Little extra flair there,
I heard that.

00:00:29.234 --> 00:00:33.601
[ Imitates a cat purring ]

00:00:33.601 --> 00:00:35.300
[ Notes play ]
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.567
You put a little extra.
-Put a little English on it.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.934
-Yeah. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.434
It's the holidays.
-Yeah a little sprinkle, man.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.033
[ Clears throat ]

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:46.634
Thank you, "House of Gucci"
or as I like to call you

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:48.634
Italian succession.

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:51.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Hey!

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:55.367
-It's good.
-What's a matter for you?

00:00:56.834 --> 00:01:00.501
-Thank you, 75% of Americans,
limiting the relatives

00:01:00.501 --> 00:01:03.501
they invite to Thanksgiving
because of COVID

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:05.300
or as 100% of them put it,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.367
"Yeah, we're not inviting
them because of COVID."

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:13.467
Sorry.
Are you vaccine?

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:17.200
Yeah. Oh, we don't want anybody
who's vaccine.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.934
Did you get your booster?
-We're celebrating the 26th.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:23.300
-The 26th we're gonna be there.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.434
You know, where Walmart is?

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:26.868
We'll be celebrating
that parking lot.

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:29.300
We'll meet you there,
don't worry about it.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.334
-You're going to celebrate
Thanksgiving in Walmart?

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:34.234
-Yeah.
-Noice! [Nice]

00:01:34.234 --> 00:01:37.701
Noice! That's righteous.

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:43.367
-Thank you, Adele's "30," for
being the official soundtrack

00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:46.167
of staring out a window with
your hand against the glass.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:49.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.701
-[ Vocalizes ]

00:01:52.701 --> 00:01:54.300
-It's out.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:00.834
Thank you, booster shots,
to be a good thing for society,

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.334
but sounding like a tequila,
you give to toddlers.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.501
-For teething. For teething.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.467
-Thank you, calling someone
on their birthday,

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:14.968
for being 10 seconds
of excitement,

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.834
followed by 10 minutes
of awkwardness.

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:19.634
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:23.267
-Happy birthday.
-Uh, did they already sing?

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:28.767
Thank you,
moving walkways at airports,

00:02:28.767 --> 00:02:30.467
for being the best way
of getting to my gate

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.601
exactly 14 seconds faster.

00:02:32.601 --> 00:02:37.400
[ Laughter, Applause ]

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:43.467
Thank you,
KitchenAid stand mixer,

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:46.767
for making sure I can't make
baked goods until I can deadlift

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.033
all 400 pounds of you
onto my counter.

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:50.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.267 --> 00:02:51.934
-[ Grunts ]

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.133
[ Imitates crash ]

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:57.501
-Gosh.
-Oh, where's the blades?

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:59.367
-Is that the last one?
-What was that?

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:02.701
-That's the last.
-Yes.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.133
-Thank-you note,
Tariq's gonna be here for,

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:06.634
like, a month or two.
-Yeah, that's right.

00:03:06.634 --> 00:03:09.133
I'm going to miss Tariq, man.
I'm going to miss you, bud.

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:10.334
-I'm going to miss you, too,
man.

00:03:10.334 --> 00:03:15.567
-I mean, [muffled chanting]

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.667
Speech.
-From me?

00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:19.634
[ Audience starts chanting
"Speech" ]

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.767
-I mean, you know, listen.
-They want one.

00:03:22.767 --> 00:03:25.334
Wow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:28.901
Alright.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:32.400
You know, at the top of,
of one mountain

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.801
represents the bottom
of of the next.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:39.234
-Oh, my goodness never mind.
-Wow!

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:42.534
-Boo! Boo! [ Laughs ]
-I really, you know.

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:46.534
[ Laughs ]

00:03:46.534 --> 00:03:49.901
-Your high school yearbook quote
or something? No.

00:03:49.901 --> 00:03:51.367
-Too good.
-It's too good.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:54.701
-It's too good.
-To be.

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.200
Wait a minute.
Is this really the last one?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.968
-Yeah.
-Oh, well, I didn't know.

00:03:59.968 --> 00:04:02.801
-Thank you, cornucopias
for being baskets

00:04:02.801 --> 00:04:04.234
that are bad at their job.

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:05.968
There you have it, everybody,
those are "Thank You Notes!"

